WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.640
In 1978, in Oldham, a baby girl
called Louise Brown was born.

2
00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:12.690
She was the first baby conceived by IVF:
an egg fertilised in a lab, in glass.

3
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:17.730
Today, eggs and sperm can be donated,
and a baby can even be carried by another

4
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:18.740
woman.

5
00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:23.370
So if a couple cannot have a
baby, how far should science help,

6
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.160
and who should decide?

7
00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:29.050
In this mission, you'll see the
main ways to overcome infertility,

8
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.040
and the questions they raise.

9
00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:36.360
Then you'll weigh a big claim: does
everyone have the right to have a child?

10
00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:40.280
Your mission: weigh up how far
fertility treatment should go,

11
00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:41.800
and who should decide.
